    /// Live updates. What changed for the active profile since `after`, held until something has.
    ///
    /// Plain HTTP long polling, as Watch together's, so every client can
    /// follow, Roku included. A signed-in client asks without `after` for
    /// the `cursor` to start from, then asks again with the cursor of each
    /// answer as soon as it arrives. With `after`, the answer waits until
    /// an event the active profile hears exists, at most 25 seconds, then
    /// answers with those events, oldest first, or with none.
    ///
    /// An event names what changed by kind and ids, never by title. The
    /// client reads the change through the ordinary operations, which
    /// decide what its profile may see, and refreshes what it shows
    /// without a spinner or a scroll jump. Events are scoped: a profile
    /// hears of its own watch state and playback sessions, of the
    /// playlists it owns or is shared, of the stations it may see and of
    /// the Watch togethers listWatchTogethers finds. An event naming an item the
    /// profile's kid filter hides is never sent to it.
    ///
    /// A client hears the kinds watch_state, playback, station,
    /// watch_together and playlist, and of the later kinds only those it
    /// names in `kinds`: a kind added to EventKind is only ever sent to a
    /// client that asks for it. The cursor moves past events of a kind
    /// not asked for as past those of another profile.
    ///
    /// The server keeps the last 512 events in memory. `resync` is true
    /// when `after` cannot be continued, being from before a restart or
    /// further back than that: the client reloads all it shows and
    /// follows on from `cursor`. A client stops asking while signed out,
    /// locked or in the background. On return it asks again with its last
    /// cursor, which the server continues from or answers with `resync`,
    /// or it reloads once and starts again without `after`. A failed poll
    /// is retried with a growing delay.
